A file is told where to read from at every read.

Mednafen's file object remembers where the file is and skips the seek when it
believes the file is already in place. A savestate brings that belief back
but not the file's own position, which the sandbox does not keep in a state:
a game loading from its disc after a state was loaded read the wrong sectors
(Virtua Fighter Remix, a state taken at frame 750 and loaded at 1125, went a
different way 165 frames later). The seek is now made before every read.

--- a/src/FileStream.cpp
+++ b/src/FileStream.cpp
@@ -289,6 +289,15 @@
  uint8* tmp_data = (uint8*)data;
  uint64 tmp_count = count;
 
+#if defined(CHIMERA_CORE)
+ // chimera: say where to read from every time. This object skips the seek
+ // when it believes the file is already there; after a savestate is loaded
+ // that belief is the state's and the file is wherever the run had left it.
+ // A read is only made with the buffer used up, so "pos" is the place.
+ if(!need_real_seek)
+  lseek(fd, pos, SEEK_SET);
+#endif
+
  while(tmp_count > 0)
  {
   const ssize_t rti = std::min<uint64>(SSIZE_MAX, tmp_count);
